  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 308476,
  "published": "2026-09-25T21:31:57.917Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version alignment with Fuuga 1.0.25 (drift-monitoring and training-safety fixes: sustained drift now keeps alerting instead of going quiet after one window, and `fuuga decide train` refuses to overwrite the checkpoint it trained from); no functional changes in Fuuga.Image (none since 1.0.19). PREVIOUS (1.0.19) — PERFORMANCE: MCP server mode keeps the most recently used diffusion and caption models resident between tool calls — previously every tool call paid a full model load (the dominant fixed cost of a generation) because the dispatcher re-entered the one-shot CLI paths; models reload only when the model path or its options change. Weights are no longer force-re-quantized to Q5_1 on load: the default is now `native` (keep the weight file's own type), which loads faster and stops silently changing quality; pass --quantization to opt into a conversion, and img2img finally accepts --quantization at all. --batch N is now implemented rather than parsed-and-discarded: N candidate images generate on ONE model load, each with a distinct reported seed, enabling a preview-then-refine flow (--batch 4 --steps 12, pick the best, re-run its --seed with full steps — generation is seed-deterministic). The MCP txt2img tool exposes the same via a `batch` argument. All diffusion commands accept --threads (physical-core count is usually fastest for stable-diffusion.cpp). Model load time is now reported (\"Model ready in Nms\") — it was previously invisible next to generation time. Dependencies: Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntimeGenAI 0.15.0 (captioning runtime), FSharp.Core 10.1.302.",
